From: XR1710G Community
Subject: mac80211: report decap offload enabled-state accurately to the driver

When a station keeps fast-rx (assign=true) while the vif lost
IEEE80211_OFFLOAD_DECAP_ENABLED, the driver callback was invoked
with assign=true even though the station decap flag was just
cleared, leaving the hardware translation enabled against the
mac80211 state. Pass assign && offload.
---
--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -4865,7 +4865,8 @@
 		set_offload = test_and_clear_sta_flag(sta, WLAN_STA_DECAP_OFFLOAD);
 
 	if (set_offload)
-		drv_sta_set_decap_offload(local, sdata, &sta->sta, assign);
+		drv_sta_set_decap_offload(local, sdata, &sta->sta,
+					  assign && offload);
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&sta->lock);
 	old = rcu_dereference_protected(sta->fast_rx, true);
